+
+Numbers in option positions (cluster sizes, ports, replication factors, column defaults) and interval/duration literals are kept, since replay needs them to be valid. DDL string values that replay cross-references (Kafka topics, upstream databases, connection hosts) are replaced with a stable `redacted_<hash>` token instead of the inert placeholder, so each original lines up everywhere it is used. The hash is salted with a per-run random value, so the tokens cannot be reversed by a dictionary attack on the shared output.
+
+Bound query parameters (`$1`, `$2`, ...) are redacted to `<REDACTED>`; at replay time these are bound as `NULL`, consistent with how redacted SQL literals are handled.
 
